# Code Conventions

This document summarizes the code conventions to follow in the AgriFlow project.

## TypeScript

- Use English for all code and documentation
- Always specify types explicitly
- Avoid using `any`
- Use PascalCase for classes and components
- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and methods
- Use kebab-case for file and directory names
- Use UPPERCASE for constants and environment variables

## Svelte Components

- One component per file
- Name files using PascalCase (Button.svelte)
- Type all props
- Define props at the top of the component
- Use slots for composition

## Styles

- Use TailwindCSS for styling
- Avoid inline styles
- Use clsx/tailwind-merge for conditional classes

## Tests

- Use EXCLUSIVELY Vitest for tests
- Import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest'
- Name test files *.spec.ts or *.spec.js
- Use vi.fn() and vi.spyOn() for mocks
- Follow the AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)

## Git

- Commit format: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`
- Allowed types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore
- Subject: present tense imperative, no capital first letter, no period at the end
- Follow GitFlow for branch management
